# ABP Timing

## Using IClock
```csharp
public class MyService : ITransientDependency
{
    private readonly IClock _clock;

    public void DoSomething()
    {
        var now = _clock.Now; // Use instead of DateTime.Now
    }
}
```

## In Base Classes
`ApplicationService`, `DomainService` have `Clock` property:

```csharp
public class BookAppService : ApplicationService
{
    public void CreateBook()
    {
        var creationTime = Clock.Now;
    }
}
```

## Configuration
```csharp
Configure<AbpClockOptions>(options =>
{
    options.Kind = DateTimeKind.Utc; // or Local
});
```

## Why Use IClock?
- Consistent time handling across application
- Testable (can be mocked)
- Supports UTC/Local configuration
